Instruction: Read the following segments of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best captures the bring down timing requirement for representations and warranties.\nQuestion: When are representations and warranties required to be made according to the bring down provisions in the Agreement?\nOption A: At Closing Only\nOption B: At Signing & At Closing\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 4.2 states that all representations and warranties of the Company, except those expressly designated as 'as of a specific event,' shall be true and correct as of the Closing Date (Page 45).\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 8.3 clarifies that, notwithstanding Section 4.2, the representations and warranties set forth in Article III of this Agreement, as modified by the subsequent Amendment, shall be valid both at the time of signing and at the Closing Date, thereby requiring them to be made at Signing and reaffirmed at Closing (Page 89).
Choices:
